{"id": "section-body-05137", "title": "Immune Reconstitution Inflammatory Syndrome (IRIS)", "chapterId": "chapter-six", "blocks": [{"id": "body-05137", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading2", "text": "Immune Reconstitution Inflammatory Syndrome (IRIS)", "runs": [{"text": "Immune"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Reconstitution"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Inflammatory"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Syndrome"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(IRIS)"}], "level": 2, "list": {"level": 1, "numberingId": "1741"}}, {"id": "body-05138", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "IRIS is a phenomenon associated with the occurrence or worsening of opportunistic infections/malignancies which can occur early after initiation of ART or at later (several months) during ART. There is an increased risk for occurrence of IRIS in the following situations:", "runs": [{"text": "IRIS"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "phenomenon"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "associated"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "with"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "occurrence"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "or"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "worsening"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "opportunistic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "infections/malignancies"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "which"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "can"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "occur early after initiation of ART or at later (several months) during ART. There is an increased risk for occurrence of IRIS in the following situations:"}]}, {"id": "body-05139", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Treatment naïve patients", "runs": [{"text": "Treatment"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "naïve"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patients"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1699"}}, {"id": "body-05140", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Patients with advanced HIV disease with CD4 cell count <50cells/mm3", "runs": [{"text": "Patients"}, {"text":